    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The second position of the verb (Verbzweitstellung)",
     "texto": [
      "In German, the order of the elements is flexible, but the conjugated verb is fixed in **second position**:",
      "1. **Subject in position 1 (direct order):**",
      "**Ich wohne in Berlin.** (Position 1: Ich | Position 2: wohne | Position 3: in Berlin).",
      "**Carlos kommt aus Spanien.** (Position 1: Carlos | Position 2: kommt | Position 3: aus Spanien).",
      "2. **Another element in position 1 (inversion):**",
      "If you put the place or the object at the beginning, the subject goes **immediately after the verb** (position 3), because the verb does not move from position 2:",
      "**In Berlin wohne ich.** (Position 1: In Berlin | Position 2: wohne | Position 3: ich).",
      "**Aus Spanien kommt Carlos.** (Position 1: Aus Spanien | Position 2: kommt | Position 3: Carlos).",
      "**Deutsch sprechen wir in Wien.** (Position 1: Deutsch | Position 2: sprechen | Position 3: wir).",
      "Careful! In German you cannot say «*In Berlin ich wohne*»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
